{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Take for Me a heifer.</b> To cut a covenant, and so that the words of the decree — which is accompanied by an oath that cannot be annulled — may stand, as the Sages of blessed memory explained (Rosh HaShanah 18a). So too did Moses our master explain, saying: לֹא בְּצִדְקָתְךָ... כִּי בְּרִשְׁעַת הַגּוֹיִם יְהֹוָה מוֹרִישָׁם וּלְמַעַן הָקִים אֶת הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע וְכוּ' אַתָּה בָא לָרֶשֶׁת (Deuteronomy 9:5)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The lemma cites only עגלה but the verse names three animals; Sforno takes the command as a whole for covenant-making."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:18.267933366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}